------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party tools invoked as separate programs (NOT part of this source distribution)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

intelligent-release-image-staging distributes and stages software images — and
builds its optional IOx application packages — by INVOKING the following tools as
separate, independent programs (subprocesses). It does not link against, embed,
include, or derive from their source code. Each tool is executed via its own
command-line / RPC interface and remains under its own license:

  * aria2c   — GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPLv2).
               A fully-static binary is FETCHED AND VERIFIED AT BUILD TIME
               (see tools/get-aria2c.sh and server/Dockerfile); it is NOT part
               of this source repository and is NOT redistributed in source
               form here. The server communicates with it only over its JSON-RPC
               interface and command line.

  * mktorrent — GNU General Public License, version 2 (GPLv2).
               Installed as a system package and invoked as a subprocess to
               create .torrent metadata.

  * openssl  — Apache License, Version 2.0 (OpenSSL 3.x).
               Installed as a system package and invoked as a subprocess
               (e.g. to generate secrets and TLS material).

  * ioxclient — Cisco IOx Client — proprietary Cisco software distributed by
               Cisco Systems, Inc. under its own license terms. It is
               operator-provided (staged at tools/bin/ioxclient or pointed to by
               the IOXCLIENT variable), which keeps IOx package builds working in
               air-gapped environments, and is invoked only as a separate
               command-line program to build the optional IRIS IOx application
               packages (iris-arm64.tar / iris-amd64.tar). It is NOT part of this
               source repository and is NOT redistributed here.

